ORDINANCE - 3rd READING - Amending Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, Chapter 10.80,
Bicycles, of the Cheyenne City Code for the purpose of removing certain chapter sections relating
to bicycle licensing requirements.  Major Dorr spoke regarding bicycle safety; bicyclists obeying
rules of the road and bicycle owner responsibility.  He requested the ordinance continue to remain
in effect and that each applicant for a license receive a copy of City Code (Chapter 10.80)
concerning operating bicycles within the City, and a pamphlet on bicycle safety.  During his
comments, Mr. Dorr submitted a copy of City Code Chapter 10.80 and a sample of the pamphlet he
had received from the Wyoming Department of Transportation (on file with City Clerk’s office).
Reporting for Finance Committee, Mr. Brown moved to approve on third and final reading, seconded
by Mr. Luna.  Comment was made concerning bicyclists’ responsibility involving safety and
compliance with laws, and using licensing fees collected per the current ordinance for bike path
costs.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present with the
exception of Ms. Williams voting “no”.  (#4116)
ORDINANCE - 3rd READING - Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, Tract 318,
Sunnyside Addition, 7 Filing, Laramie County, Wyoming (located at the northwest corner of the
th
intersection of Polk Avenue and Rock Springs Street).  Reporting for Public Services Committee,
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Roybal.  Motion carried.
Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present. (#4117)
ORDINANCE - 3rd READING - Pursuant to Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendments,
Section 5.1.2, Zoning Districts Established, and Section 5.1.3, Official Zoning Map, of the Unified
Development Code, changing the zoning classification from County CB Community Business to
MR-2 Medium-Density Residential-Developing for a portion of PKT Subdivision, within Tract 318,
Sunnyside Addition, 7 Filing, Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming (located at the northwest
th
corner of the intersection of Polk Avenue and Rock Springs Street).  Dr. Rinne moved to approve
on third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Johnson.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members
of the governing body present. (#4118)
ORDINANCE - 3rd READING - Pursuant to Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendments,
Section 5.1.2, Zoning Districts Established, and Section 5.1.3, Official Zoning Map, of the Unified
Development Code, changing the zoning classification from LI Light Industrial to HI Heavy
