the governing body present. (#4119)
ORDINANCE - 2nd READING - Amending Section 2.40.035(B), Traffic School-
Administrative Fee, of Chapter 2.40, Municipal Court, of Title 2, Administration and Personnel, of
the Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming.  Ed Strader spoke in opposition to the fee increase,
commenting on municipal court and trainer costs and expressing the proposed fee increase is
excessive.  Mr. Brown moved to approve on second reading, seconded by Ms. Williams.  Mr.  White
moved to amend by changing the proposed administrative fee from $25.00 to $40.00 with the fee
not to exceed $60.00, seconded by Ms. Williams.  Discussion followed on the intent of the
amendment, and consideration of a friendly amendment was offered to remove the “not to exceed
```

### Page 3 of 6

```text
$60.00" clause from the amendment.  Pursuant to inquiry from Mr. Strader, it was advised that if the
fee were to be changed in the future, it would require governing body approval.  Mr. White, as maker
of the motion, accepted the friendly amendment and indicated his revised motion was to change the
current $25.00 administrative fee to $40.00, and to eliminate language regarding “not to exceed
$60.00”.  As second to the motion to amend, Ms. Williams concurred. Discussion included:
Procedurally entertaining motions to amend an amendment as has been the practice of the governing
body; leaving latitude of determining when to increase the administrative fee to the municipal court
judge, and administrative fee only affecting violators who the court believes would benefit from
traffic school attendance.  The Honorable Mark Moran, Municipal Court Judge, described
components and benefits of the traffic school program and advised that the program is labor
intensive to administer so that is the reason for requesting an increase in the administrative fee. He
noted it had been 11 years since the fee has been reviewed and the intent of requesting an amount
not to exceed $60.00 was to gradually increase the fee over time, beginning with an increase to
$40.00.  Judge Moran explained program costs to participants and that it is a voluntary option for
eligible individuals, and reviewed options to violators regarding payment of fines, appearing in court
or attending the program.  Motion to amend failed.  Voting “no” -- all members of the governing
body present.  Mr. Shanor moved to amend by changing the administrative fee to be in an amount
not to exceed $50.00 instead of $60.00, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Discussion included program fees;
ticket costs, and the program providing an incentive for people to attend by having a ticket dismissed
upon successful completion of the program.  Motion to amend carried.  Voting “yes” -- Mr. Brown,
Mr. Johnson, Mr. Luna, Mr. Shanor and Mayor Kaysen.  Voting “no” -- Dr. Rinne, Mr. Roybal, Mr.
White and Ms. Williams. Main motion as amended carried.  Voting “yes” -- Mr. Brown, Mr.
Johnson, Mr. Luna, Mr. Shanor and Mayor Kaysen.  Voting “no” --  Dr. Rinne, Mr. Roybal, Mr.
White and Ms. Williams voting “no”.
ORDINANCE - 1 READING - Amending Section 10.32.030, Decreasing State Speed
ST
Limits in Certain Zones, of Chapter 10.32, Speed Limits, of Title 10, Vehicle and Traffic, of the
Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming -- referred to Public Services Committee (sponsors -- Mr.
Brown, Dr. Rinne and Mr. Shanor).
RESOLUTION - Amending the Neighborhood Traffic Management Program (NTMP) - 2015
which was adopted by Resolution No. 5657.  Dr. Rinne moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Roybal.
Dr. Rinne moved to amend by substitute, seconded by Mr. Roybal.  Pursuant to inquiry regarding
the substitute, Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk, clarified the resolution itself is not being amended and
that the substitute pertains to a proposed revision of the NTMP document affiliated with the
resolution.  Upon inquiry, Tom Mason, Director, Metropolitan Planning Organization, summarized
the proposed changes contained in the substitute NTMP document as a result of a meeting between
administrative staff and certain Council members.  He explained most of the changes were simple
edits and reviewed the main highlights that were included in the substitute.  Motion to amend
carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present.  Main motion as amended
carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present. (#5743)  Under other business,
Jeff Dierksen, spoke in reference to the NTMP changes, noting he thought some of the changes were
an improvement but others were not.  He commented in opposition to the speed watch portion of the
program and expressed concern that certain data collecting methods may be misleading and
suggested the governing body review this section further.
