[CA]
RESOLUTION - Authorizing the Mayor and the City Clerk to sign a Final Plat for PKT
Subdivision, a replat of Tract 318, Sunnyside Addition, 7 Filing; and Lot 2, Sunnyside Meadows,
th
Cheyenne, Wyoming (located at the northwest corner of the intersection of Polk Avenue and Rock
Springs Street).  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried. (#5744)
RESOLUTION - Adopting the Dell Range/Prairie Avenue/Section 20 Corridor Study.  Dr.
Rinne moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Roybal.  Inquiry followed regarding the rationale of
narrowing lanes from four to two lanes on Prairie Avenue, and installing a roundabout at Prairie and
Frontier Mall Drive instead of utilizing traffic signals and the cost difference.  Darci Hendon, Ayres
Associates, explained that Prairie Avenue projected future traffic volumes doesn’t justify a four lane
street and that even with future projected growth, only one lane in each direction is necessary. She
noted that roundabouts keep traffic moving, not stopping at signals.  John Hall, City Engineer,
advised the estimated cost of traffic signals would be approximately $250,000 - $300,000 dollars
where as the roundabout would cost approximately $2 million.  He noted a roundabout may qualify
for federal funding through the Metropolitan Planning Organization process to help with the cost,
and stated a roundabout is a better long term solution.  Comment was made that Melton Street should
“go all the way through”.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body
present with the exception of Dr. Rinne voting “no”. (#5745)
