th
Luna.  Upon inquiry regarding using MOU’s as a standard operating procedure where developers
are swapping land in lieu of park fees, Rick Parish, Director of Parks and Recreation, explained that
the developer will pay the fees and reimbursement would be made when certain provisions are met
as outlined in the MOU.  He noted the MOU was in conjunction with the Final Plat and a condition
of approval of the plat required the MOU to come before the governing body.  Discussion followed
on amenities and improvements to be provided by the developer.  Upon inquiry, Dan White, City
Attorney, explained the reason for deeding the land is to change ownership to the City, but under
MOU provisions the developer is to make certain improvements to qualify for fee reimbursement.
He advised some of the improvements will be on privately owned land; provided information
